# Core Algorithm

## cascadeDown()

This became the most important algorithm inside Planner.

Purpose

```
Create one free slot
inside requested bucket.
```

Example

Before

```
Critical

A
B
C
```

Insert

```
X
```

Result

```
Critical

A
B
X
```

```
High

C
```

Algorithm

```
Current Bucket Full

↓

Next Bucket Full?

↓

Recursively cascade next bucket

↓

Move last node to next bucket

↓

Normalize current bucket
```

Maximum recursion depth

```
5
```

No planner rows are deleted.

Only

```
priority
priorityOrder
```

are updated.

---

# Important Architecture Decisions

## Planner rows are never recreated

Earlier approach

```
Delete

↓

Insert
```

was rejected.

Final implementation

```
Update Existing Row
```

Benefits

* preserves nodeId
* preserves todayOrder
* preserves timestamps
* avoids unnecessary inserts

---

## Today Queue lives inside PlannerNodeEntity

Separate TodayQueueEntity was rejected.

Reason

One entity already stores

```
todayOrder
```

which completely represents Today's Queue.

---

## Normalization

Normalization always occurs after removal.

Never before.

Destination buckets never require normalization because moved nodes are appended.

---

## Cascade Philosophy

The newly added task always remains in requested bucket.

The least important task gets pushed downward.

Example

```
Critical

A
B
C
```

Insert

```
X
```

Result

```
Critical

A
B
X
```

Never

```
X
A
B
```

